# OpenLibm 0.8.8 -- provenance of the vendored libm source and the SHA-256 of
# the pinned tarball. TASK/T07 (lead decision 2026-09-21: port OpenLibm as the
# SDK's libm; mintlib never had one -- on m68k it came from the compiler).
#
# PROVENANCE
#
#     curl -L -o sdk/libm/openlibm-0.8.8.tar.gz \
#         https://github.com/JuliaMath/openlibm/archive/refs/tags/v0.8.8.tar.gz
#
# Release v0.8.8, published 2026-09-02, tag commit
# 5fe399749f9276eaa0b8403e507470da05cbbb3f (GitHub API, fetched 2026-09-21).
# The tarball is the GitHub source archive of that tag: the FreeBSD msun /
# OpenBSD libm / fdlibm 5.3 derived C sources plus per-arch asm (amd64, i387,
# ...) and the ld80/ld128 long-double directories. What of it is compiled is
# decided by sdk/libm/build-libm.sh from OpenLibm's own Make.files manifests.
#
# LICENSE
#
# sdk/libm/LICENSE.openlibm.md is a verbatim copy of the tarball's LICENSE.md
# (SHA-256 b1843fbf5b03f519a5f0a44fce751bdd1022ae7148614923f9d6293e17a18b17):
# MIT (the Julia project's standalone-library work), ISC (Stephen L. Moshier),
# 2-clause BSD (FreeBSD msun), and the SunPro fdlibm notice ("Permission to
# use, copy, modify, and distribute this software is freely granted, provided
# that this notice is preserved"), all of which the compiled sources carry in
# their headers. The LGPL notice in that file covers only test/test-double.c
# and test/test-float.c, which are not compiled into libm.a. Like the ported
# mintlib/gemlib/cflib, libm.a is an SDK artifact separate from the clean-room
# OS (ADR-019).
#
# The build script verifies the tarball against the line below before
# extracting it, and refuses to build on a mismatch.
#
# Format: <sha256>  <file relative to sdk/libm/>
721bab18ff37160fd9e903eb211ff26fdee38c3d0041d556b07d76089c435d17  openlibm-0.8.8.tar.gz
